# state-dir-propagation.manifest — KNOWN members of the #1335 class that do
# NOT yet propagate their resolved state dir to their `ng log-action` children.
#
# Read by monitor/watcher/test-state-dir-propagation.sh. A member is a shell
# file under monitor/ that RESOLVES a state dir (`STATE_DIR=…`,
# `_resolve_state_dir`, or a `--state-dir` flag) AND invokes `ng log-action`.
# It is COMPLIANT when it `export`s NEXUS_STATE_DIR, or every invocation line
# (or its `\`-continued predecessor) carries a `NEXUS_STATE_DIR=` prefix.
#
# RATCHET, in both directions: a non-compliant member NOT listed here is a
# red (a new instance of the class); a listed member that has become
# compliant, or is no longer a member, is ALSO a red (remove the line — a
# stale allowance is a permit nobody audits). One path per line, followed by
# a tab and the reason it is still here.
#
# The fix is one line per file: `export NEXUS_STATE_DIR="$STATE_DIR"` right
# after the script resolves STATE_DIR (retire-preflight.sh and
# paste-followup.sh are the worked examples). Do NOT add `--state-dir` to
# the call — `cmd_log_action` rejects it, and under a `timeout ( … )`
# subshell that is a silent per-gate failure (#1369).
